<title>USA: Bristol says Bass deal accretive.</title>
<headline>Bristol says Bass deal accretive.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bristol Hotel Co said on Monday that its acquisition of 61 hotels from Britain's Bass Plc should be slightly accretive to its earnings in 1997, excluding one-time integration and transaction costs.</p>
<p>Bristol said it will issue to Bass 9.37 million shares of Bristol common stock, purchase certain hotel assets for $91 million, and provide for the retirement of $300 million of existing intercompany debt to Bass.</p>
<p>Based on the closing price for Bristol's common stock on December 13th, the total transaction is valued at $659 million, it said.</p>
